release-me, next branch of github.com/TitusKirch/release-me

This is a modified version of release-me by Simon Ostendorf
(https://github.com/ostendorf-cloud/release-me), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). It is not an official release-me release.

The modifications integrate the following pull requests of the upstream
repository before they are released there. Every change, and the files each
one modifies, is recorded in the git history of the next branch.

- #78 fix(pr)!: create the release commit through the forge so it is signed
- #79 feat(release)!: delete the release branch once its pull request is released
- #80 feat(releasepr): turn the release pull request guide off
- #81 feat(version): add bump-patch-for-minor-pre-major
- #82 feat(components): leave subpaths out of a component with exclude-paths
- #83 feat(release): tag without a GitHub release under skip-github-release
- #84 feat(updater): add npm-lock, cargo-lock and gemfile-lock updaters
- #85 feat(version): add release-please's versioning strategies
- #86 feat(changelog): rename, reorder and add sections through changelog-sections
- #87 feat(updater): add an xml updater for pom.xml and .csproj
- #88 feat(release): create the GitHub release as a draft under draft
- #89 feat(components): allow a root component beside other components
- #90 feat(pr): configurable release pull request title patterns
- #91 feat(changelog): sentence case entries with changelog-sentence-case
- #92 feat(updater): add a plain updater for version.txt
- #93 feat(pr): a header and a footer for every release pull request body
- #94 feat(changelog): credit entry authors with changelog-authors
- #95 feat(release): add force-tag-creation to leave the tag to the release publish
- #96 feat(pr): open release pull requests as drafts with release-pull-request-draft
- #97 feat(config): add the release-as key
- #98 feat(updater): add updaters for release-please's release type version files
